1
00:03:43,199 --> 00:03:49,199
Hey dude, this is NO cartoon.

2
00:07:26,399 --> 00:07:32,399
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles is a science fiction, action,
adventure film directed by Steve Barron.

3
00:11:09,599 --> 00:11:15,599
A quartet of humanoid turtles, trained by their mentor in ninjitsu, must learn to
work together to face the menace of Shredder and the Foot Clan.

4
00:14:52,799 --> 00:14:58,799
Leonardo (voice), played by Brian Tochi.

5
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Raphael (voice) / Passenger In Cab, played by Josh Pais.

6
00:22:19,199 --> 00:22:25,199
Donatello (voice), played by Corey Feldman.

7
00:26:02,399 --> 00:26:08,399
Michaelangelo (voice), played by Robbie Rist.

8
00:29:45,599 --> 00:29:51,599
April O'Neil, played by Judith Hoag.

9
00:33:28,799 --> 00:33:34,799
Casey Jones, played by Elias Koteas.

10
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles is a 1990 American superhero comedy film based on the
comic book characters created by Kevin Eastman and Peter Laird.

11
00:40:55,199 --> 00:41:01,199
It is the first film in the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles franchise.

12
00:44:38,399 --> 00:44:44,399
Directed by Steve Barron and written by Todd W.

13
00:48:21,599 --> 00:48:27,599
Langen and Bobby Herbeck from a story by Herbeck, it stars Judith Hoag and Elias Koteas
with the voices of Brian Tochi, Josh Pais, Corey Feldman, and Robbie Rist.

14
00:52:04,799 --> 00:52:10,799
The film follows the Turtles on a quest to save their master, Splinter, with their new
allies, April O'Neil and Casey Jones, from the Shredder and his Foot Clan.

15
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
The film adapts the early Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles comics, with several
elements taken from the animated series airing at the time.

16
00:59:31,199 --> 00:59:37,199
Filming took place in 1989 in North Carolina and New York City.

17
01:03:14,399 --> 01:03:20,399
Many major studios turned down distribution for the film,
worrying that it could be a box office disappointment.

18
01:06:57,599 --> 01:07:03,599
New Line Cinema, at that time a small independent production
company, acquired the rights halfway through production.

19
01:10:40,800 --> 01:10:46,800
The turtle costumes were developed by Jim Henson's Creature Shop, one of Jim
Henson's last projects before his death shortly after the premiere.

20
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles was released theatrically in the
United States on March 30, 1990, by New Line Cinema.

21
01:18:07,199 --> 01:18:13,199
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $202 million on a budget of $13.5 million; it was the
highest-grossing independent film up to that time and the ninth-highest-grossing film worldwide of 1990.

22
01:21:50,399 --> 01:21:56,399
It was followed by Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles II: The Secret of the
Ooze (1991) and Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles III (1993).

23
01:25:33,599 --> 01:25:39,599
The film explores themes of new york city, martial
arts, skateboarding, brother, superhero.

24
01:29:16,799 --> 01:29:22,799
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
